Backend cross-checks (sources read for the migration policy):
  - internal/api/battery_handler.go (/vehicles/{id}/battery): returns _km
    distance fields and avg_cell_temp_c. Derived SI in km, NOT meters.
    NOTE: that endpoint is consumed by useBatteryHealth (not used by
    BatteryHealthPage, which calls /analytics/battery-health). Adapter
    is consistent across both: both surface km values directly.
  - internal/api/battery_degradation_handler.go (/analytics/battery-health
    and /analytics/battery-degradation): returns BatteryHealthAnalytics
    with history[] containing range_km (km), capacity_kwh (kWh), soh_pct,
    odometer (km). monthly_trend[].range_km same shape.
  - internal/api/sleep_handler.go (/analytics/sleep): preserves zero-valued
    sentry/drain keys for FE contract per Phase-42/0077; outside_temp is
    °C (SI). Page uses convertTemp(°C) which is correct for either useSettings
    or useUnits (identical behaviour for °C input).
  - internal/api/router.go:1267-1268: /vampire-drain and /vampire-drain/stats
    routes were DELETED by Phase-42/0077 (vampire_drain_events table
    dropped). VampireDrainPage and useVampireDrain* hooks call dead URLs.
  - internal/service/energy_service.go + internal/database/energy_repo.go:
    EnergyService.EnergyStats returns _mi and _wh_per_mi fields after
    SQL adapter conversion (genuine miles boundary, locked-policy
    continuation from Phase-43/0020-0022 Drive.distance_mi precedent).
  - internal/api/range_projection_handler.go (/vehicles/{id}/battery/projected-range):
    returns _km / km/h / Wh/km fields. UI is km-native by design (sliders,
    efficiency matrix, what-if scenarios all in km/h+km). User-pref
    conversion would require translating speed buckets too — deferred.

Migration policy (locked-in for this prompt):
  1. range_km (analytics) is derived SI in km. Convert via:
       convertDistanceFromSI(km * 1000, unitPrefs.distance)
     Legacy useSettings.convertDistance(km) is BROKEN here because the
     legacy helper assumes miles input and would multiply by 1.609 when
     pref is km, producing wildly wrong values. This is the same root-
     cause pattern as the Phase-43/0022 driving fix.
  2. avg_cell_temp_c, module_temp_min/max (charging telemetry) is °C SI.
     Legacy useSettings.convertTemp(celsius) is correct (identity-on-°C,
     C→F otherwise). Keep as-is; useUnits.formatTemperature is equivalent.
  3. EnergyStats _mi/_wh_per_mi fields stay on legacy useSettings.convert*
     per locked-policy continuation (Phase-43/0021 charging precedent).
  4. ProjectedRangePage _km/km/h/Wh/km display is intentionally km-native
     (the entire what-if calculator UX assumes km buckets). Migration
     deferred to a dedicated audit; the page remains functional and
     consistent with itself.
  5. Vampire-drain page surfaces existing error UI when the dead endpoints
     return 404. Page IS preserved per ADR-005 #1 / si-cutover rule 5;
     not stubbed, not deleted. Documented in code comment for future
     resurrection if backend grows replacement signals.


