=== PAGE_PORT ===
Per-page outcome (10 pages):

1. BatteryHealthPage.tsx - PORTED.
   Bug fix: 4 sites previously called useSettings.convertDistance(km_value)
   on backend range_km (km) values. The legacy helper expects MILES input,
   so users with unit_of_length=mi saw the value times 1.609 (showing km
   numbers labelled mi); users with km saw the number unchanged but mis-
   labelled in callers that read distanceUnit. Migrated to
   convertDistanceFromSI(km * 1000, unitPrefs.distance) via a useCallback
   fromKm helper.
   Sites:
     - line ~292 rangeTrend chart data
     - line ~841 'Range When New' card
     - line ~852 'Range Now' card
     - line ~858 'lost' delta
   Display unit label switched from distanceUnit (legacy useSettings) to
   unitPrefs.distance (useUnits), which is identical at the value level
   ('mi'|'km') but sourced from the SI-canonical hook for consistency.
   Charging telemetry temperature reads (lines ~564/581/611-614) intentionally
   keep useSettings.convertTemp(C) - backend's module_temp_min/max is
   already C SI and the legacy convert is identity-on-C / C->F otherwise,
   identical to convertTempFromSI.

2. BatteryDegradationPage.tsx - PORTED.
   DataTable column renderers previously hardcoded ' km' on range_km and
   odometer. Migrated both to fromKm(km) + unitPrefs.distance. Same
   fix-pattern as #1.

3. BatteryCellsPage.tsx - UNCHANGED.
   Renders cell voltages (V) and pack temperatures (C). No SI conversion
   needed for V; temperature reads already pass through useSettings.convertTemp
   which handles C -> F correctly. Page uses inline request<T> instead
   of useBatteryCells - left as-is to avoid scope creep (DRY clean-up
   would touch unrelated rendering paths).

4. EnergyFlowPage.tsx - UNCHANGED for SI.
   Backend daily_breakdown[].distance_mi is genuine miles after SQL
   adapter (locked-policy precedent from Phase-43/0021 charging port).
   Existing legacy toDisplayDistance(mi, DistanceUnit.Miles, userDistUnit, 1)
   is correct. Migration to useUnits would require routing miles ->
   metres at the call site for no behavioural change. Deferred.

5. EnergyPage.tsx - UNCHANGED.
   Uses useEnergyStats whose total_distance_mi is genuine miles
   (locked-policy). Existing useSettings.convertDistance(mi) already
   correct.

6. EnergyProductsPage.tsx - UNCHANGED.
   Tesla Energy site product cards. No vehicle SI fields; W/kWh display
   via existing helpers.

7. PowerFlowDashboardPage.tsx - UNCHANGED.
   Powerwall live status (W and Wh). No user-pref distance/temperature
   fields.

8. ProjectedRangePage.tsx - UNCHANGED.
   Backend returns _km/km/h/Wh/km and the page is km-native by
   design (speed sliders, efficiency matrix buckets, what-if scenarios
   all built around km). A meaningful port to mi would need translated
   speed buckets (e.g., 35 km/h ~= 22 mph but the matrix axis is in 5 km/h
   steps) and a Wh/mi efficiency table. Treating this as a deferred
   policy decision - page remains internally consistent and functional.

9. SleepEfficiencyPage.tsx - UNCHANGED.
   convertTemp(event.outside_temp) is called on C SI which the legacy
   helper handles correctly.

10. VampireDrainPage.tsx - UNCHANGED (intentionally surfaces 404).
    Endpoint /vampire-drain/stats was deleted by Phase-42/0077. Page
    already wraps the useQuery result in error/empty UI via the
    error prop, so the user sees a graceful "data unavailable"
    state instead of a blank panel. Per ADR-005 #1 and si-cutover
    rule 1, the page is preserved (not stubbed, not deleted, not
    EmptyState-fronted). The dead URL is documented in code as a
    @deprecated hook; a future prompt can resurrect via signal_log
    (BatteryLevel + IdleNumberOfMinutes) without any front-end work
    beyond rebinding the page to useSleepEfficiency-style aggregates.

