=== NOTES ===
1. Bug-fix scope: this prompt corrects a pre-existing bug where the analytics
   range_km field (km, derived SI) was passed to the legacy
   useSettings.convertDistance helper which expects MILES input. Symptom
   for users with unit_of_length=mi: range was multiplied by ~1.609,
   showing e.g. "850 mi" for a Model 3 packing ~530 km of range. Symptom
   for unit_of_length=km users was less obvious - the value passed
   through unchanged but the fixed distanceUnit literal was 'km' so the
   user saw the right number with the right unit "by accident". After
   this prompt both prefs render the same true value via
   convertDistanceFromSI(km * 1000, unitPrefs.distance).

2. Locked-policy continuation: per Phase-43/0020 (vehicles), 0021
   (charging), 0022 (driving), fields with explicit _mi / _mph suffix
   that are converted at the SQL adapter boundary stay on legacy
   convertX helpers because the values are GENUINE miles after the
   boundary. EnergyService.EnergyStats total_distance_mi /
   avg_efficiency_wh_per_mi and daily_breakdown[].distance_mi follow
   this rule. Only true canonical SI fields (_km derived SI from
   signal_log; _c Celsius; _kpa kPa; _m metres) get migrated to
   convertXFromSI.

3. Vampire-drain dead endpoints: /vampire-drain/stats and
   /vampire-drain were removed by Phase-42/0077 alongside the
   vampire_drain_events table drop. The hooks useVampireDrainStats
   and useVampireDrainEvents are still in useEnergy.ts because the
   dashboard VampireDrainWidget (out of scope for this prompt - lives
   under web/src/features/dashboard/) still imports them. The hooks
   are now @deprecated-tagged with a future-replacement plan that
   derives the same metrics from signal_log (BatteryLevel +
   IdleNumberOfMinutes). VampireDrainPage gracefully surfaces the 404
   via the useQuery.error prop - no UI hiding, no EmptyState
   substitution, page is preserved per ADR-005 #1.

4. ProjectedRangePage deferral: the page is km-native by design
   (efficiency matrix in 5 km/h speed buckets, what-if calculator
   built around wh_km, range scenarios labelled km). A meaningful
   migration to mi requires translating the entire bucket scheme and
   adding a Wh/mi efficiency column - substantial UX work that exceeds
   "port to new SI shapes" scope. Documented for a follow-up audit.

5. Type-source decision: stayed on web/src/types/energy.ts rather than
   the partial web/src/api/types.ts. The latter declares an EnergyStats
   interface with total_distance_km / avg_efficiency_wh_km claiming
   SI - but the backend handler internal/service/energy_service.go
   plus the SQL adapter internal/database/energy_repo.go actually emit
   total_distance_mi / avg_efficiency_wh_per_mi. types/energy.ts
   matches the backend reality. Realigning api/types.ts is OUT OF SCOPE
   for this prompt (allowed-files list excludes it) and would be wrong
   to do unilaterally on the FE side anyway - a future prompt should
   migrate the backend to emit _km AND update both type files together.

6. PowerShell gate workarounds: the prompt's verbatim audit grep regex
   parses correctly only when the surrounding string interpolation does
   not contain a backtick before another backtick (which is treated as
   an escape sequence). The audit was factored into a temporary script
   gate-audit-temp.ps1 (cleaned up pre-commit) using ["\x27] notation
   for the single-quote/backtick/double-quote character class. Same
   logical check, different parser-survival.

7. PowerShell here-string trap: $-prefixed strings inside an expandable
   @"..."@ here-string get interpolated even when intended as literal
   placeholder text (e.g., ${vehicleId}). The PAGE_PORT/HOOK_PORT
   sections were written through a literal partial file (*.log.partial)
   then Get-Content -Raw | Out-File -Append to avoid interpolation
   collisions. Future prompts that want to embed template-literal-style
   URLs in their log should use the same pattern or an @'...'@ literal
   here-string.

8. Self-deleting gate script: the final-step git status check would
   otherwise see the gate script itself as an untracked file and emit
   STATUS=BLOCKED. Workaround per Phase-43/0021 NOTES: script removes
   itself via Remove-Item $MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path before invoking
   git status.
EXIT=0
STATUS=DONE
